{"term":"foundation","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:64746cc872bb36f3cf","definition":"The act of founding, fixing, establishing, or beginning to erect.","example":"The foundation of his institute has been wrought with difficulty.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["establishment"],"antonyms":["abolition","dissolution","ruination"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["foundational","foundationary","foundation degree","foundationed","foundationer","foundation garment","foundationless","foundation model","foundation myth","foundation stone","foundationwear","grounation","lay a foundation","microfoundation","pile foundation","refoundation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b7439b08e45339d707","definition":"That upon which anything is founded; that on which anything stands, and by which it is supported; the lowest and supporting layer of a superstructure; underbuilding.","example":"Aye Madam to be sure that is the Provoking circumstance—without Foundation—yes yes—there's the mortification indeed—for when a slanderous story is believed against one—there certainly is no comfort like the consciousness of having deserved it——","pos":"noun","synonyms":["basis","groundwork","underbuilding","underframework","warp and weft","underpinning"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["foundational","foundationary","foundation degree","foundationed","foundationer","foundation garment","foundationless","foundation model","foundation myth","foundation stone","foundationwear","grounation","lay a foundation","microfoundation","pile foundation","refoundation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b4440e9795ea6b4669","definition":"The result of the work to begin something; that which stabilizes and allows an enterprise or system to develop.","example":"The implication is that the Gandhian model of growth is possible, now that Nehru's investment strategy had already laid a strong foundation for economic growth.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["groundwork","platform","stage"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["foundational","foundationary","foundation degree","foundationed","foundationer","foundation garment","foundationless","foundation model","foundation myth","foundation stone","foundationwear","grounation","lay a foundation","microfoundation","pile foundation","refoundation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:905526a38d326e7264","definition":"In solitaire or patience games, one of the piles of cards that the player attempts to build, usually holding all cards of a suit in ascending order.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["foundational","foundationary","foundation degree","foundationed","foundationer","foundation garment","foundationless","foundation model","foundation myth","foundation stone","foundationwear","grounation","lay a foundation","microfoundation","pile foundation","refoundation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b03db5fbe9d38f8423","definition":"The lowest and supporting part or member of a wall, including the base course and footing courses; in a frame house, the whole substructure of masonry.","example":"The foundations of this construction have been laid out.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["base","groundwall"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["foundational","foundationary","foundation degree","foundationed","foundationer","foundation garment","foundationless","foundation model","foundation myth","foundation stone","foundationwear","grounation","lay a foundation","microfoundation","pile foundation","refoundation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:466697783f778c1ae3","definition":"A donation or legacy appropriated to support a charitable institution, and constituting a permanent fund; endowment.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["foundational","foundationary","foundation degree","foundationed","foundationer","foundation garment","foundationless","foundation model","foundation myth","foundation stone","foundationwear","grounation","lay a foundation","microfoundation","pile foundation","refoundation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c63d49eb8ae4f0d2fc","definition":"That which is founded, or established by endowment; an endowed institution or charity.","example":"The Wikimedia Foundation, Inc. is the parent organization of the Wiktionary collaborative project.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["foundational","foundationary","foundation degree","foundationed","foundationer","foundation garment","foundationless","foundation model","foundation myth","foundation stone","foundationwear","grounation","lay a foundation","microfoundation","pile foundatio